  "id": "multimethod-approach",
  "term": "multimethod approach",
  "definition": "A multimethod approach is a way of studying a psychological construct by combining several different kinds of measures or sources of evidence rather than relying on just one. In this packet, it refers to evaluating psychopathic traits with self-report, interview-based ratings, and behavioral, physiological, and related questionnaire measures.",
